    {
      "id": "text-150",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1140,
      "y": 1284,
      "width": 1120.0,
      "height": 160.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e9ecef",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 157326193,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1154561094,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "• Only nginx listens on a public interface: :80 answers 301 → https, :443 terminates TLS (cert in ./certs).\n• The gateway is not published: nginx is the only way in, and it forwards /api/ only (/internal, /actuator stay unreachable).\n• tweet- and timeline-service trust X-User-Id blindly, so they must stay reachable through the gateway alone.\n• Infra ports stay bound to 127.0.0.1: reachable from the host itself or an SSH tunnel, never from the internet.\n• No shared .env: each container gets only the variables it reads (mail-service never sees JWT_SECRET or MinIO keys).\n• Session cookie HttpOnly · SameSite=Strict · Secure; SPA and /api share one origin, so there is no CORS.\n• Email links are built from PUBLIC_URL.  kafka-ui and mailpit start only with --profile dev.\n• TLS: certbot --standalone on the host, copied to ./certs, renewed by hand every 90 days.",
      "originalText": "• Only nginx listens on a public interface: :80 answers 301 → https, :443 terminates TLS (cert in ./certs).\n• The gateway is not published: nginx is the only way in, and it forwards /api/ only (/internal, /actuator stay unreachable).\n• tweet- and timeline-service trust X-User-Id blindly, so they must stay reachable through the gateway alone.\n• Infra ports stay bound to 127.0.0.1: reachable from the host itself or an SSH tunnel, never from the internet.\n• No shared .env: each container gets only the variables it reads (mail-service never sees JWT_SECRET or MinIO keys).\n• Session cookie HttpOnly · SameSite=Strict · Secure; SPA and /api share one origin, so there is no CORS.\n• Email links are built from PUBLIC_URL.  kafka-ui and mailpit start only with --profile dev.\n• TLS: certbot --standalone on the host, copied to ./certs, renewed by hand every 90 days.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
